BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In a Landscape
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T183000
UID:260504gNQlM_xJKUyIln-PiSvQrQ
DESCRIPTION:Founded in 2016 by classical pianist Hunter Noack\, IN A LANDS
 CAPE: Classical Music in the Wild is a 501\\(c\\)\\(3\\) nonprofit outdoor
  concert series where America's most stunning landscapes replace the tradi
 tional concert hall. A 9-foot Steinway grand piano travels on a flatbed tr
 ailer to State and National Parks\, urban greenspaces\, working ranches\, 
 farms\, and historical sites for classical music concerts that connect peo
 ple with each landscape. To meet the acoustical challenges of performing i
 n the wild\, music is transmitted to concert-goers via wireless headphones
 . No longer confined to seats\, audiences explore the landscape\, wander t
 hrough secret glens\, lie in sunny meadows\, and roam old growth forests. 
 IN A LANDSCAPE has presented 275 concerts in Oregon\, Washington\, Montana
 \, Idaho\, New York\, Utah\, Wyoming\, and California to over 55\,000 peop
 le. Folks travel from near and far. Local ranchers\, loggers\, and farmers
  gather with visiting city dwellers and tourists from beyond.  Get your ti
 ckets HERE
LOCATION:Campovida
URL:https://www.campovida.com/upcoming-events/in-a-landscape/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boogie for Good
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T200000
UID:260504MdkjWWuqt0GnxKphZoVEIg
DESCRIPTION:Audacity Rising is proud to present our next big event of the 
 season. This rousing show will feature Dirty Cello\, an Internationally ac
 claimed Americana band bringing their version of rockin' covers of the 60'
 s and 70's with some of their own original material. They bring a high ene
 rgy concert not to be missed! The opening band for our headliner will be n
 one other than Tom Rigney and Flambeau\, one of the nation's finest and mo
 st accomplished Zydeco and Cajon Bayou bands known everywhere for their to
 p-of-the-line musical styles and exceptional musicianship\, not to mention
  some of the finest Cajon Fiddle and beautiful violin playing known to gra
 ce the stage. As always\, the proceeds will go to benefit the legal defens
 es of our marginalized immigrant communities who need the services provide
 d to them by our own North Bay's dedicated and gifted legal partners VIDAS
  (Vital Immigrant Defense and Advocacy Services).
LOCATION:Friedman Event Center
URL:https://audacityrisinginc.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:INTO THE LIGHT: Light-filled aintings by Katy Boggs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T170000
UID:260501hY6p_PaXH0qk4c6yuE8LYQ
DESCRIPTION:Katy's paintings are an exploration of light—how it shapes f
 orm\, reveals color\, and defines what we see.\n\n"I am drawn to moments w
 here light is felt as much as seen: filtering through dense leaves\, tower
 ing in the crowns of trees\, glinting off cresting waves\, or softening in
 to the quiet glow of a sunset. Light is everywhere\; without it\, there is
  no seeing. Beyond its physical presence\, it also carries a deeper resona
 nce as a symbol of hope. In a time of uncertainty\, this work seeks to bri
 ng light into the image\, both visually and metaphorically."\n\nReception:
  April 25\, 4 to 6 pm.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Gallery
URL:http://sebastopolgallery.com
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In a Landscape - Classical Music in the Wild
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T170000
UID:2604255IeKE6AqVEqr5Q8-4T3dZA
DESCRIPTION:For the 11th season\, IN A LANDSCAPE: Classical Music in the W
 ild tours the American West. Mountain tops\, old-growth forests\, and sunn
 y meadows replace the traditional concert hall in the series featuring pia
 nist Hunter Noack on a 9-foot Steinway concert grand piano. Listen through
  wireless headphones and wander afield with the music as a soundtrack to y
 our experience in the wild.\n\nAbout this Landscape\n\nSet along a gentle 
 creek in the tiny hamlet of Hopland\, Campovida is a family-owned farm and
  winery. Lavender gardens guide guests to the concert site\, a meadow fram
 ed by a pair of oak trees. Organic and biodynamic farming practices connec
 t the 150 acres of orchards and gardens to the rich agricultural legacy of
  the Pomo people in the ancestral Sanel Valley of southeastern Mendocino C
 ounty.\n\nTurn your concert into a wine-country weekend with a stay at Tha
 tcher Hotel or Stock Farm Hotel\, both located just one mile from Campovid
 a in Hopland. Explore nearby wineries\, restaurants\, and small-town shops
  with guidance from Visit Ukiah as you plan your visit.\n\nWith thanks to 
 Thatcher Hotel\, Stock Farm Hotel\, and Visit Ukiah for their support of t
 his concert.\n\nConcert FAQs:\n\nAccessibilityThe pathway to the concert s
 ite\, will be approximately a 15 minute walk from a paved parking lot\, to
  a dirt path\, through an organic garden and field with some uneven terrai
 n.\n\nSeatingBring your own chairs or blankets.No seating provided.\n\nFoo
 d & BeveragesDrinks and light snacks will be available for purchase. Outsi
 de food and drink are not permitted.\n\nDogsNot allowed at Campovida Winer
 y.\n\nSmokingProhibited at all IN A LANDSCAPE concert sites.\n\nRefunds & 
 CancellationsAll ticket purchases are final. There are no refunds unless I
 N A LANDSCAPE cancels the performance. The show goes on regardless of weat
 her.
LOCATION:Campovida
URL:https://visitukiah.com/events/in-a-landscape-classical-music-in-the-wi
 ld/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:An Abstract Vision
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T110500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260524T170000
UID:2604244UtZVP7UFke6dUo2JOc7ww
DESCRIPTION:Abstract art moves beyond representation\, with a strong empha
 sis on shape\, color and form. Abstract art has the power to evoke emotion
 s\, appeal to our senses and transcend the physical world. Abstract expres
 sion captures the delicate\, elusive\, powerful and radiant energies that 
 fly under the radar of explanation.\n\nExhibition Artists: Dahlo (Marcela 
 Cabrera)\, Tess Abts\, Erika Adkins\, Bev Barnett\, Tara Belkin Harvey\, C
 ynthia Brodie\, Deborah Chaney\, Sharon Crary\, Alyson Dobbert\, Dianne Je
 an Erickson\, Kristine Goldenberg\, Beth Hall\, Sarah Harvey\, Ann Kalb-Ki
 p\, Debra Kreck­Harnish\, Michelle Nishikatsu\, Katy Parks Wilson\, D. Mi
 mi Read\, Elizabeth Springs\, Carol Tacconi\, Deborah Titus\, Chris Vetran
 o\, Mike Wasden\, Kim Winter\, Tara Yellen\, Kay Young\, Sabina Zildzic
LOCATION:Healdsburg Center for the Arts
URL:https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/an-abstract-vision/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
