BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The 68th Annual Sonoma Valley Joint Memorial Day  Observance
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260525T140000
UID:2605226LFa4jqv9E69NTFQUnTs3g
DESCRIPTION:The Sonoma Valley community will gather at 11:00 a.m. on Monda
 y\, May 25\, at Sonoma Veterans Memorial Park for the 68th Annual Sonoma V
 alley Joint Memorial Day Observance\, presented by the Sonoma Veterans Mem
 orial Park Association.\n\nThis year’s Guest of Honor and keynote speake
 r will be retired United States Marine Corps Colonel Harry “Bucky” Pet
 erson\, a Sonoma resident and distinguished 33-year Marine Corps veteran w
 hose service included combat and leadership assignments in Vietnam\, the M
 iddle East\, Somalia\, Kuwait\, Iraq\, and Afghanistan. During his militar
 y career\, Colonel Peterson commanded units ranging from rifle platoons in
  Vietnam to an entire Marine Infantry Regiment. Following his retirement i
 n 1999\, he returned to active duty after the September 11 attacks to help
  oversee Marine operations in Afghanistan and Iraq. His military honors in
 clude the Distinguished Service Medal\, the Defense Superior Service Medal
 \, two Legion of Merit awards\, and three Combat Action Ribbons.\n\nThe ce
 remony will include the traditional Grand March of Veterans\, with all vet
 erans encouraged to arrive by 10:30 a.m.\, as seating is limited. Addition
 al program highlights will include patriotic performances by the Sonoma Ho
 metown Band under the direction of Therese Pasquale Hill\; Color Guard pre
 sentations by both the United States Marine Corps and the Civil Air Patrol
  Cadet Color Guard\; and a Rifle Salute presented by local veterans’ org
 anizations.\n\nMusical tributes will feature the National Anthem performed
  by Miss Sonoma County 2026 Addison Carver\, “God Bless America” sung 
 by vocalist Cathy Slack\, and ceremonial selections by bagpiper John Noona
 n and bugler Therese Pasquale Hill. Korean War veteran Olyn Hicks will pre
 sent a Memorial Day poem\, while regional pageant titleholders will lead t
 he Pledge of Allegiance.\n\nAdditional participants will include Sonoma Ma
 yor Ron Wellander\, who will deliver an official proclamation\; Vietnam ve
 teran Gene Campagna\, who will offer the invocation\; and Reverend Peadar 
 A. Dalton\, who will deliver the benediction. The ceremony will also featu
 re a civilian aerial flyover provided by the Sonoma Sky Park Aviators.\n\n
 Serving as Master of Ceremonies will be Carl “Chip” H. Allen\, a gradu
 ate of the United States Naval Academy and former U.S. Navy Polaris submar
 ine officer.\n\nImmediately following the ceremony\, guests are invited to
  attend the complimentary “All-American Picnic” hosted by the three So
 noma Rotary Clubs and the Native Daughters of the Golden West at the Sonom
 a Veterans Memorial Building.\n\n Guests will also have an opportunity to
  contribute to the ongoing Star of Honor pledge drive\, which supports the
  preservation of Sonoma Veterans Memorial Park and its black marble Star o
 f Honor Fountain — a lasting tribute inspired by the late World War II N
 avy veteran James “Jim” L. Parks.
LOCATION:Sonoma Veterans Memorial Park
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/the-68th-annual-sonoma-
 valley-joint-memorial-day-observance/18903461/2026-05-25T11
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
