BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Beginner Salsa - Tuesdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T183000
UID:2603191k0BDVjt306Hl6ZAWUjXKA
DESCRIPTION:Ready to dance? Join our beginner salsa class where no experie
 nce or partner is needed. Just comfortable shoes and desire to have fun!\n
 \nGreat for first timers!\n\nNo dance experience required\n\nNon-marking s
 hoes soles\n\nNo partner necessary\n\nOur relaxed environment is perfect f
 or learning salsa basics\, as we make it fun and enjoyable. In this class 
 you will learn basic directional steps\, proper frame for partner-work and
  simple turn patterns. We organize our curriculum so that the movements ar
 e easy to remember. Join us to learn the fundamentals! No experience is ne
 cessary and no partner is required. Drop-in fee is $20.\n\nDate & Time: Tu
 esdays @ 5:30PM – 6:30PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafae
 l\, CA\n\nNote: Arrive 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allo
 wed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/beginner-salsa-tuesdays
 /17157360/2026-05-26T17
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Intermediate Salsa Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T193000
UID:260318ZkBfLv1MlE-YCdfywwRpWA
DESCRIPTION:This class is designed for dancers who have a solid grasp of t
 he basics and are eager to expand their repertoire with more complex and f
 luid movements.\n\nPre- requisite:\n\nSalsa Class Beginners\n\nEach week\,
  we’ll break down a new move\, focusing on the technique and connection 
 that will make you a more confident and stylish dancer. We’ll go beyond 
 the foundational steps to cover a wide range of essential intermediate pat
 terns and styling\, including:\n\nTurns and Spins:\n\nMaster your inside a
 nd outside turns\, double spins\, and the elegant 360 and Hand Toss moves.
 \n\nIntricate Patterns:\n\nLearn to execute the 360\, wrap\, as well as va
 rious Cross Body Lead variations like the U-Turn and Spiral.\n\nFootwork a
 nd Styling:\n\nEnhance your rhythm and flair with advanced footwork like t
 he Suzy Q\, Front Tap\, and Mambo Step. We’ll also work on styling with 
 a wrap and improving your posture and upper body movement.\n\nThis class i
 s your chance to refine your technique\, improve your lead-follow connecti
 on\, and add a variety of fun and dynamic moves to your salsa vocabulary. 
 Join us and elevate your dance!\n\nDetails:\n\nNo partner necessary — ro
 tations ensure everyone gets to dance.\n\nPlease wear non-marking shoe so
 les to protect the floor.\n\nArrive 10 minutes early to warm up and get s
 ettled.\n\nDate & Time: Tuesdays @ 6:30PM – 7:30PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/intermediate-salsa-clas
 s/17159571/2026-05-26T18
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:John Craigie
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T000000
UID:260224vhopS8YT00C3-cZ9yH0_OQ
DESCRIPTION:For over a decade\, John Craigie has made music that brings pe
 ople in. Not with spectacle\, but with sincerity and songs that feel like 
 conversations.\n\nI Swam Here\, Craigie’s forthcoming studio album is du
 e February 6\, 2026 via Zabriskie Point Records. Much of the album\, recor
 ded in New Orleans in January 2025\, finds Craigie backed by musicians han
 dpicked by Sam Doores of The Deslondes. With him on piano\, organ and voca
 ls he brought along Howe Pearson on drums\, Max Bien Khan on bass\, Jonny 
 Campos on pedal steel and an appearance by Desiree Cannon on vocals on one
  track.  Longtime friend and collaborator\, Anna Moss\, appears on almost 
 every song. While Craigie served as producer you can feel the influence an
 d the talents of the New Orleans musicians on the seven of the ten tracks 
 that were recorded there. The other three songs were recorded a few months
  later at the Rope Room up in Astoria\, Oregon with a different band but m
 irroring the aesthetic of the New Orleans sessions. The cover art\, painte
 d by B. Schall\, who herself has spent time living in New Orleans\, mirror
 s the style and design of many samba and jazz records of the 50s and 60s.\
 n\nThe record’s first single\, “Fire Season\,” was engineered by lon
 gtime collaborator Bart Budwig. This was one of  the first songs written f
 or the project and was recorded in Astoria with Cooper Trail on drums and 
 Nevada Sowle on bass\, both returning after working with Craigie on Mermai
 d Salt. It also has Luke Ydstie on bass \\(Blind Pilot\, Michael Hurley\\)
  and Jamie Greenan on pedal steel.\n\nThe second single “Dry Land” too
 k a different path. They recorded a version in New Orleans but Craigie did
 n’t like the pacing and it had a long unneeded bridge.  It was re-record
 ed in Astoria a few months later with a different piano line and a bowed u
 pright bass.\n\nThe 3rd upcoming single\, “Edna Strange” is inspired b
 y the songs of Marty Robbins and other western gunfighter ballads. This is
  the only song where Craigie plays steel string acoustic.  Max Bien Khan i
 s doing the nylon string guitar leads.  One of the few songs to not featur
 e Anna Moss vocals\, instead they opted to reference Marty Robbins with th
 e male trio vocal you can hear in the background\,\n\nFollowing 2024’s P
 agan Church — his acclaimed collaboration with TK & The Holy Know-Nothin
 gs that spent 6 weeks at \\#1 on the Americana Albums charts— I Swam Her
 e feels both expansive and intimate\, drawing from the musical history of 
 the Gulf Coast and the quiet natural sounds of the Pacific Northwest.\n\nC
 raigie’s music continues to resonate far beyond the studio. He has packe
 d out solo and band tours across the U.S.\, Europe and Australia\, perform
 ed at Newport Folk Festivals\, Pickathon\, Edmonton Folk Festival\, and Hi
 gh Sierra\, and shared the stage with Langhorne Slim\, Brett Dennen\, Sier
 ra Hull\, Gregory Alan Isakov\, Mason Jennings\, Bella White\, and Jack Jo
 hnson. His annual \\#KeepItWarm Tour donates $1 from every ticket sold to 
 regional nonprofits fighting food insecurity\, while his beloved John Crai
 gie On the River trips on the Tuolumne \\(CA\\) or Rogue \\(OR\\) rivers h
 ave become a one-of-a-kind gathering for fans and friends alike.\n\nI Swam
  Here is another step forward for Craigie. Rooted in place\, shaped by col
 laboration\, and guided by his steady hand as a songwriter and producer. I
 t blends the spirit of New Orleans with the stillness of the Pacific North
 west\, and shows the quiet confidence of an artist who is still exploring 
 his limits.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107705660?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Napoleon Dynamite Live A Conversation with Jon Heder\, Efren Ramir
 ez\, and Jon Gries
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260526T193000
UID:2605056aAQlJPIvE-n6ZR5I_rseQ
DESCRIPTION:Since the release of the beloved indie classic\, Napoleon Dyna
 mite\, 20 years ago\, much has changed\, but the characters\, as enduring 
 as they are endearing\, stay in our hearts. This unique evening includes a
  full screening of Napoleon Dynamite\, followed by a lively discussion wit
 h cast members\, Jon Heder \\(Napoleon Dynamite\\)\, Jon Gries \\(Uncle Ri
 co\\)\, and Efren Ramirez \\(Pedro\\). Perfect for the whole family\, this
  live show is a wild and hysterical blend of Q&A\, comedy improv\, game sh
 ow\, and party\, with plenty of audience participation.\n\nVIP Meet and Gr
 eet Add-On Option:\n\nElevate your event experience with this exclusive ch
 ance to meet Jon Heder \\(Napoleon\\)\, Efren Ramirez \\(Pedro\\)\, and Jo
 n Gries \\(Uncle Rico\\)\, including a photo opportunity. With limited tic
 kets available\, be sure to reserve yours soon!
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1403736727710624/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
