DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the rich cultural traditions of Mexico through the v
 ibrant artistry of the musicians and dancers in LBC's afterschool Marichi 
 and Ballet Folklórico programs atVoces y Pasos \\(Voices and Steps\\): A 
 Cultural Celebration. Featuring more than 150 of Sonoma County's talented 
 youth\,Voces y Pasosbrings these traditions and celebrations to life in an
  unforgettable stage performance that pays tribute to their Mexican herita
 ge. LBC's Mariachi Ensemble and its sister program\, LBC's Ballet Folklór
 ico\, enroll students from all over the county. Together they deliver stun
 ning performances that blend technical skill\, stage presence\, and heartf
 elt expression while embodying the grace and vibrancy of traditional Mexic
 an folk music and dance. The young performers in these programs devote the
 mselves to weekly rehearsals and regular performances at community events 
 that continue to shape them into impressive artists. Thanks to the generos
 ity of our donors and sponsors\, they can participate at no cost to their 
 families\, with all equipment and costumes provided. Join us for an inspir
 ing evening that shines the spotlight on the voices and steps of these tal
 ented students and honors the enduring power of culture\, tradition\, and 
 community.
LOCATION:Datoire Foundation
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/voces-y-pasos-a-cultural-celebration/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cheese & Butter Classes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T170000
UID:260520s0I8IqZPh0aW_D14fby_Kg
DESCRIPTION:Join award-winning cheesemaker Sheana Davis and wine expert Be
 n Sessions for unforgettable cheese and butter making classes. Perfect fo
 r team building\, celebrations\, and educational events\, our classes are 
 interactive\, fun\, and easy for everyone. \n\nFrom classes on how to make
  Creme de Ricotta wheel to Mozzarella Pulling to butter-making classes\, g
 uests will always leave with a creamy treat to take home \\(if it makes it
  that far!\\) – so bring a small cooler with you.  \n\nFood has a remar
 kable ability to bring people together. \n\nCheesemaking classes are perfe
 ct for team-building activities\, company meetings\, team celebrations\, s
 taff events\, corporate fun\, bridal parties\, couples classes\, girlfrien
 d getaway weekends\, LGBT events\, EBT education courses\, and more. Class
 es held year-round on Thursday\, Friday\, and Saturday\, 12:00-2:00 and 3:
 30-5:30pm. \n\nSee the full schedule of all our cheese and butter making c
 lasses here.  \n\nWith each class\, we give back to the community by prov
 iding meals for food-insecure seniors in Sonoma Valley. After learning how
  to make cheese\, our guests can prepare these meals and write personal no
 tes for the seniors on the lids.  \n\nJoin us in making a positive impact
  while having fun and learning a new skill.   \n\nYour Cheesemaking Expe
 rience: \n\n\n\nBegin with local wine and an artisanal cheese tasting.\n\n
 Learn to make cheese and compound butter with everyday ingredients and too
 ls.\n\nEnjoy specialized classes for dishes like lasagna and gourmet grill
 ed cheeses.\n\nExclusive guest cheesemakers often share their techniques.\
 n\nIdeal for corporate events\, bridal parties\, getaways\, and more.\n\n\
 n\nSheana and Ben pride themselves on using ingredients readily available 
 in any local grocery store\, with cooking supplies used reside in most hom
 e cooks’ kitchens. Guest cheesemakers are often available to showcase th
 eir own cheeses and techniques\, making the class a truly unique experienc
 e. \n\nCheck the schedule for Wine Country-based cheesemaking classes.  
 \n\nCustomize Your Class:To arrange private or corporate classes at venues
  like Sonoma Fairmont Mission Inn or Silverado Resort\, contact us at she
 anadavis@gmail.com. We can help create a unique and unforgettable experien
 ce for your entire group! Private and corporate classes may be arranged an
 d are hosted at various Wine Country venues\, including The Fairmont Sonom
 a Mission Inn\, Silverado Resort\, The Lodge in Sonoma\, and private homes
  and estates. \n\nTo register: \n\nhttps://theepicureanconnection.com/even
 ts/
URL:https://www.farmtrails.org/event/cheese-butter-classes/2026-05-28/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Belly Dancing with Raja
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260528T183000
UID:2604204nZiMZ7HLUWOPw6AUQECgA
DESCRIPTION:Unlock your inner strength and find your flow. Belly dancing 
 with Raja is an innovative fusion class that blends the rhythmic artistry 
 of belly dance with the high-energy benefits of aerobics. Designed to b
 e both a cardiovascular challenge and a deep toning session\, this class f
 ocuses on the “powerhouse” of the body—your core.\n\nBy layering flu
 id\, isolative movements over an athletic aerobic base\, you will challeng
 e your muscles in ways traditional gym workouts can’t reach.\n\nWhat to 
 Expect\n\n• Core-Centric Power: Use undulations and shimmies to engage 
 deep abdominal muscles for a tighter\, stronger midsection.\n\n• Functio
 nal Stability: Improve your balance and posture through controlled\, hip-
 driven movements and low-impact aerobic footwork.\n\n• Total Body Toning
 : Build lean muscle in your legs\, glutes\, and arms while maintaining a 
 constant\, heart-pumping pace.\n\n• Mind-Body Connection: Enhance your 
 coordination and body awareness through rhythmic\, expressive choreography
 .\n\n“Whether you’re looking to define your waistline or simply want a
  workout that feels like a celebration\, this class offers the perfect bal
 ance of sweat and grace.”\n\nDifficulty Level: All levels welcome! No p
 rior dance experience is required—just bring your energy and a willingne
 ss to move.\n\nDATE AND TIME: Thursdays at 5:30 PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/belly-dancing-with-raja
 /18622402/2026-05-28T17
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
