BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aging with Grace: A Yoga Retreat for Adults 50 plus
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260529T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260529T200000
UID:250917Zu71nztkfUiaEn1fGcGSdA
DESCRIPTION:Aging with Grace: A Yoga Retreat for Adults 50 plus - Step int
 o a joyful weekend of movement\, relaxation\, and renewal\, thoughtfully d
 esigned for adults 50 and anyone who like this idea!\n\nBook now and get $
 100.00 off listed prices. Offer valid until Feb 27\, 2026\n\nhttps://yourh
 ealthandjoy.com/retreatmay2026/\n\n$895.00 – For 1 Guest in a Private Ro
 om \\(Shared Cottage\\)\n\nWe welcome back Guest Teacher Patricia Becker\,
  beloved for her uplifting yoga and wellness teachings\, to host a retreat
  that will rejuvenate your body\, calm your mind\, and rekindle your natur
 al vitality.\n\nThis retreat tends tends to fill quickly—secure your spo
 t today!\n\nStep into a joyful weekend of movement\, relaxation\, and rene
 wal\, thoughtfully designed for adults 50 and better.\n\nAs the seasons sh
 ift and nature begins to blossom\, this retreat invites you to do the same
 —reconnect with your strength\, flexibility\, and inner glow.\n\nWith a 
 nourishing blend of yoga\, breathwork\, meditation\, and meaningful connec
 tion\, you’ll explore ways to move with greater ease\, feel content\, an
 d age with grace. Whether you’re seeking more energy\, deeper calm\, or 
 simply a pause from routine\, this weekend offers the space to replenish\,
  reset\, and return home to yourself.\n\nYou’ll stretch\, strengthen\, a
 nd smile your way through sessions supporting joint health\, posture\, spi
 nal alignment\, hip mobility\, deeper breathing\, and overall vitality—n
 o pretzel poses required!\n\nPlayful curiosity and gentle guidance will he
 lp you tap into your body’s wisdom and celebrate what’s possible at ev
 ery age.\n\nWhat to Expect:\n\nUplifting yoga to build strength\, balance\
 , and mobility\n\nBreathwork and meditation to calm your mind and restore 
 energy\n\nTime in nature to reflect\, rest\, and restore\n\nDelicious vege
 tarian meals lovingly prepared\n\nConnection with like-hearted people in a
  warm and welcoming space\n\nPlenty of time to laugh\, lounge\, and be ful
 ly yourself\n\nHear what Guests have to say!\n\n“I loved the invigoratin
 g Aging With Grace Retreat at beautiful Ratna Ling — which I attended wi
 th a few fellow Yoginis. I’m planning to return for more of Patricia’s
  gentle but powerful yoga\, uplifting commentary\, and lovely yoga communi
 ty.” — Desiree Petray\n\n“I’m not a senior but I wanted gentle yog
 a and a relaxing weekend with time for introspection. I learned so much ab
 out my body and breath\, and met amazing new friends. Patricia is knowledg
 eable\, kind\, and made the experience fun.” — Ruby Williams\n\n“My 
 sister and I adored Patricia’s yoga retreat. The minute you arrive you k
 now it will be special. Patricia creates a sense of community and offers j
 ust the right amount of stretching and strengthening. You feel graceful—
 like you’ve been enveloped by unconditional love.” — Ann Protter\n\n
 Retreat Schedule \\(subject to change\\):\n\n\\* Friday – Arrive \n\n3:
 00 PM – Check-in and Settle in \n\n4:30–5:30 PM – Root & Release: Y
 oga for Your Feet & Ankles Gently land at Ratna Ling and reconnect with yo
 ur foundation through soothing stretches and grounding breath. \n\n5:30
 –6:15 PM – Dinner \n\n6:45–8:00 PM – Opening Circle & Centering P
 ractice Meet your fellow retreat guests and ease into retreat mode with li
 ght movement\, intention-setting\, and calming breathwork.\n\n\\* Saturday
  – Stretch\, Strengthen & Soften \n\n8:00–8:45 AM – Breakfast \n\n
 9:00–10:00 AM – Release & Realign: Yoga for Neck & Shoulders Let go of
  upper-body tension and invite ease and openness. \n\n11:15 AM–12:15 PM
  – Lengthen & Decompress: Yoga for a Healthy Back Support your spine wit
 h mindful movement to restore strength and flexibility. \n\n12:15–1:00 
 PM – Lunch \n\n1:00–4:30 PM – Personal Time Walk\, journal\, nap\, 
 read\, or enjoy a bodywork session. \n\n4:30–5:30 PM – Freedom to Mov
 e: Yoga for Hips & Hamstrings Stretch and strengthen the lower body for gr
 eater balance and mobility. \n\n5:30–6:15 PM – Dinner \n\n7:00–8:0
 0 PM – Glow & Unwind: Face Yoga \\+ Restorative Yoga A sweet blend of fa
 cial toning and deeply restful poses to help you relax and restore.\n\n\\*
  Sunday – Integrate & Renew \n\n8:00–8:45 AM – Hands\, Wrists & Sel
 f-Compassion Flow Care for your hands and wrists while cultivating presenc
 e and self-kindness. \n\n9:00–10:00 AM – Head-to-Toe Stretch & Closin
 g Circle Seal in the weekend’s gifts with a full-body flow and heartfelt
  closing. \n\n10:00–11:00 AM – Brunch \n\n12:00 PM – Check-out\n\n
 Facilitator- Patricia Becker Patricia Becker is a certified yoga teacher a
 nd nutrition expert with decades of experience in yoga\, breathwork\, and 
 holistic wellness. Patricia specializes in teaching live online yoga class
 es for adults 50\\+\, including both chair yoga and mat-based practices. S
 he also works one-on-one with clients to support strength\, flexibility\, 
 balance\, and overall well-being. Patricia is passionate about helping oth
 ers feel their best—physically\, mentally\, and emotionally. Show me mor
 e https://yourhealthandjoy.com/ Learn more about Patricia Becker\n\nBathe 
 in the joy of yoga with stretching and strengthening poses as well as brea
 th awareness meditation. Expect a playful practice of self-acceptance and 
 exploration at the beautiful Ratna Ling.\n\nGreat for those who\n\n• are
  new to yoga \n\n• feel stiff\n\n• want to slow down and care for you
 rself\n\n• want greater agility\n\n• want a stronger healthier back\n\
 n• want to be more flexible\n\n• want to maintain mobility\n\n• like
  good company\n\nFRIDAY\n\n3:00pm               Check-in\n\n4:30-5
 :30pm       Arrive Here at Ratna Ling ~Yoga for Your Feet and Ankles 
 \n\n5:30-6:15pm       Dinner\n\n6:45-8:00pm       Opening Circle -
  \n\nSATURDAY\n\n8:00-8:45am         Breakfast\n\n9:00-10:00am    
    Loosen and Relax ~Yoga for Your Neck and Shoulders\n\n11:15am-12:15pm
  Lengthen and Decompress~  Yoga for a Healthy Back\n\n12:15-1:00pm    
     Lunch\n\n1:00-4:30pm         Quiet time\, hiking\, journaling\,
  reading\, or bodywork by appointment\n\n4:30-5:30pm        Mobility -
  Happy Hips and Hamstring Yoga\n\n5:30-6:15pm        Dinner\n\n7:00-8:
 00pm        Face Yoga and Restorative Yoga \n\nSUNDAY\n\n8:00-9:00  
      Yoga for Your Hands and Wrists\n\n9:00-10:00      Head to Toe S
 tretches and Closing Circle\n\n10:00-11:00am Brunch\n\n12:00pm        
     Check out\n\nPatricia Becker is a Yoga\, Breath and Diet Coach with 
 40 years experience of study\, practical experience and coaching. \n\nCer
 tified Yoga Alliance RYT®  E-RYT®.  Patricia has a Yoga TV Show\, YouT
 ube Channel\, Live Online Programs. \n\nShe was a Yoga Instructor for Sta
 nford's Health Improvement Program for 11 years. Learn More at https://you
 rhealthandjoy.com/
LOCATION:Ratna Ling Retreat Center
URL:https://yourhealthandjoy.com/retreatmay2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
