BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Author Event: Italianity by Jessica Dupuy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260601T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260601T180000
UID:260523vtubtAwOhkG5CNv_LK6BBQ
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special event with Jessica Dupuy\, author of Ita
 lianity. This event is free\, but we appreciate your RSVP below so we can 
 plan for your attendance. ABOUT THE BOOK Italy's vineyards stretch from Al
 pine peaks to volcanic islands\, from rolling Tuscan hills to sun-drenched
  coastlines. Each glass of Italian wine carries not only the flavor of its
  land but also the imprint of centuries of tradition\, community\, and cul
 ture. Italianity is a groundbreaking exploration of that soul. Written by 
 Andrea Lonardi\, one of Italy's most respected winemakers\, agronomists\, 
 and a rare Master of Wine\, together with acclaimed wine journalist Jessic
 a Dupuy\, this book traces the cultural thread that unites Italy's native 
 grapes and the people who cultivate them. From the misty hills of Piedmont
  and the Alpine slopes of Alto Adige to the volcanic soils of Sicily and t
 he olive groves of Tuscany\, Italianity brings readers face to face with t
 he landscapes\, families\, and traditions that make Italian wine unlike an
 ything else on earth. Through vivid storytelling\, unforgettable encounter
 s\, and cultural reflection\, Lonardi and Dupuy reveal how Italian wine is
  more than a beverage: it is history and heritage\, innovation and resilie
 nce\, the rhythm of the seasons\, the joy of the table\, and a way of seei
 ng beauty in the everyday. "Italianity brilliantly reveals how Italian win
 e is inseparable from Italian culture. Drawing on his deep vocation and ex
 pertise\, Andrea Lonardi and Jessica Dupuy present a beautifully written e
 xploration of wine as both heritage and daily life. This book arrives at a
  pivotal moment\, as Italy's native grapes are being preserved and reinter
 preted through new technology. With passion and precision\, they show why 
 Italian wine is not just a drink\, but a living expression of culture. Bra
 vo!" — Shelley Lindgren\, Owner A16 restaurant and Author\, Italian Wine
 \, A16 Food Wine\, SPQR\, San Francisco\, CA ABOUT THE AUTHOR Jessica Dupu
 y is an award-winning wine journalist whose work appears in Food & Wine\, 
 GuildSomm\, SevenFifty Daily\, and Forbes. A certified sommelier and autho
 r\, she brings an expert yet approachable perspective to wine storytelling
 .
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1717997385861471/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
