BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Summertime Livin' Easy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T180000
UID:260519xsfjLSzdiUi--d0pSyE6rQ
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  5/15/26\n\nJUNE EXHIBIT: SUMMERT
 IME LIVIN’ EASY\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  June 1 – June 28\, 2026\n\nRECEPTI
 ON: SATURDAY\, June 6\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Nancy Gray  and Ga
 llery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show and the Gal
 lery’s 29th anniversary.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free 
 monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments
  will feature the Gallery’s signature mocktail: Brushstroke Fizz.\n\nSon
 oma County artist\, Nancy Gray\, unveils new summer-inspired acrylic paint
 ings that are a colorful expressive interpretation of the region’s beaut
 y.  Summer is the artist’s favorite season and it shows. Drawing inspir
 ation from the French Fauvist tradition\, these works abound with interpre
 tive color choices and bold brush work.  Non-literal color expression pla
 ys out in “Evening Shade” as backlit trees cast blue tendrils of shade
  dancing on a bed of reddish ground.  Sprinkled across a carpet of golden
  yellow\, vibrant red poppies glow in “Sundrenched Splendor\,”amplifyi
 ng the heat of the midday sun.  Red poppies take on a dramatic contrastin
 g role in “Lavender Fields Forever” as they play against the purplish 
 blues and lavenders of the fields and sky.  Inspired by the landscape\, t
 hese works reinterpret it through emotion and memory.  “We are blessed 
 to live amongst Sonoma’s breathtaking scenery – everywhere I look\, I 
 see a painting\,” noted Gray.\n\nGray has had a lifelong passion for art
 .  A Texas native\, she loves living in wine country with its inspiration
 al landscapes.  Along with the Fauvist painters\, early years vacationing
  on the Caribbean Coast and Belize influenced her bright color palette.  
 She began exhibiting her art in Houston in the early 90’s and continued 
 to focus on her painting after moving to Sonoma County.  Gray exhibits re
 gionally and has been a member of the Upstairs Art Gallery for five years.
 \n\nMeet the artist: Gray will host the Gallery on June 18 and 25 from 11a
 m to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Collective Express
 ions: 29 Years\, a members’ collaborative show celebrating the Gallery
 ’s 29th anniversary. Gallery artists offer an exciting mix of mediums\, 
 subject matter and styles emblematic of the Gallery’s dynamic diversity.
   Landscapes by Barretta\, Laland\, and Zorich highlight our region’s b
 eauty\; travel afar with Bird’s Paris cityscape\; from sunflowers to ros
 es\, flowers star in works by Gray\, Haley\, Miller\, Schaffer\, Sumner an
 d Wilson\; succulent oranges are the focus of Stolper’s stunning still-l
 ife\; lovable pets are the subject of Tobin-Charleston’s jewelry\; abstr
 acts by Morgan and Reid bring a moving contemporary complement\; figurativ
 e works by Rapp\, Roney and Shore round out this classic to contemporary o
 verview of the Upstairs artistic family.\n\nAlso join us for ART NITE HEAL
 DSBURG\, Thursday\, June 4\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 
 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and cre
 ativity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\n
 Upstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\
 ) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    www.upstairsart gallery.net 
 \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bv
 drio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Doug Ferrari Live
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T220000
UID:26051990c1YXTyR0yIHwGTql2JFg
DESCRIPTION:Doug Ferrari—affectionately known as “Dougzilla”—has b
 een a larger-than-life presence in American comedy\, both on and off the s
 tage. Born on Christmas Day in 1956 in San Francisco\, his journey has bee
 n anything but typical. A gifted student\, he graduated from High School a
 t just sixteen and boldly chose to follow his passion for making people la
 ugh over attending Stanford University even though he had a full scholarsh
 ip.\n\nThat leap of faith paid off quickly. After his first stand-up perfo
 rmance at The Comedy Store\, Doug co-founded the musical comedy group High
  Wire Radio Choir\, releasing Teenage Mutant Love in 1979 and Guys From 
 Space in 1983. By 1984\, he had won the prestigious San Francisco Comedy C
 ompetition and was performing 500 shows a year. Along the way\, he shared 
 the stage with legends like Jerry Seinfeld\, Drew Carey\, Robin Williams\,
  and Bob Hope\, and opened for iconic musicians including Ray Charles\, El
 vis Costello\, and Sun Ra.\n\nDoug’s talent extended beyond the stage\, 
 with television appearances on HBO\, Showtime Comedy Club Network\, Evenin
 g at the Improv\, VH1’s Stand-Up Spotlight\, MTV’s ½ Hour Comedy Ho
 ur\, and the ABC series A Fine Romance. \n\nHe also contributed his writi
 ng skills to comedy greats such as Jay Leno on The Tonight Show and Rodney
  Dangerfield for many years and still writes for comedians.\n\nWhile his j
 ourney included significant personal challenges\, Doug’s resilience beca
 me one of his defining strengths. After stepping away from comedy in the 1
 990s\, he made a powerful return in 2000—bringing not only his humor bac
 k to audiences but also a deep commitment to helping others.  Let him te
 ll it:\n\n“I am neurodiverse. I have managed medicated depression\, gene
 ralized anxiety disorder\, and I’m a recovering drug addict since 1994\,
  so addictive personality and impulsivity. I was diagnosed as autistic at 
 60 years old. It was a big surprise until I started writing my film projec
 t about my life\, “Blood on rhe Clown Suit” and I realized I can remem
 ber EVERYTHING from the age of three.\n\nI am also autistic AF. Don’t be
 lieve me? I was first onstage age four in a pro musical not a school play.
  I can sing almost any cartoon or TV show theme song 60’s to 70’s. I h
 ave never driven a car. I have never played a video game. I have never see
 n porn. I have never played sports and I only watch the Giants. I have nev
 er had children.  Chess champion age 13\, national at speech and debate 
 champion age 16. SF international Comedy Competition\, back when it meant 
 something\, age 24. \n\nMaybe I peaked early.”\n\nToday\, he is activel
 y involved in benefits\, homeless outreach and appears in \\#BeRobin the 
 Movie\, a documentary inspired by Robin Williams and led by Margaret Cho\,
  reflecting his dedication to compassion\, connection\, and giving back.\n
 \nDoug Ferrari’s story is ultimately one of passion\, perseverance\, and
  purpose—proof that even the toughest chapters can lead to meaningful an
 d inspiring new beginnings.
LOCATION:Mac's at 19
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/doug-ferrari-live/18934
 849/2026-06-04T20
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cuban Salsa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260604T203000
UID:260518IoFpg-FDbkaFWlz4fl5yUA
DESCRIPTION:Cuban Salsa Class with Eric Celestino & Abigail Celestino\n\n4
 week class\n\nJune 4 – June 25\n\nThis is a beginner cuban salsa—you w
 ill learn your basic footwork and turns.\n\nIn this class\, you will learn
  the fundamentals of Cuban Salsa\, including body movement\, rhythm\, musi
 cality\, footwork\, partner connection\, and partnerwork patterns inspired
  by authentic Cuban dance culture. We focus on proper technique\, coordina
 tion\, flow\, and natural body expression\, while also building confidence
  and strong foundations.\n\nClasses are structured with:\n\n• Warm-up an
 d body movement\n\n• Footwork and rhythm exercises\n\n• Partnerwork te
 chnique\n\n• Short combinations and practical applications\n\nOur goal i
 s to help you understand how to dance salsa\, not just memorize steps — 
 developing timing\, connection\, and a comfortable\, joyful way of dancing
 .\n\nCome dance with us\, grow your technique\, and experience the energy 
 and flavor of Cuba in a supportive and welcoming environment.\n\nBook your
  spot\n\nDate & Time:\n\n4week class\, June 4 – June 25\n\nThursdays @ 7
 :30 PM\n\nAddress: 4140 Redwood Highway \\#8 San Rafael\, CA\n\nNote: Arri
 ve 10 minutes before. No floor marking shoe soles allowed.
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/cuban-salsa/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
