BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Summertime Livin' Easy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260605T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260605T180000
UID:260519uje15WOttEWekEpjMJRi3Q
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  5/15/26\n\nJUNE EXHIBIT: SUMMERT
 IME LIVIN’ EASY\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  June 1 – June 28\, 2026\n\nRECEPTI
 ON: SATURDAY\, June 6\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Nancy Gray  and Ga
 llery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show and the Gal
 lery’s 29th anniversary.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free 
 monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments
  will feature the Gallery’s signature mocktail: Brushstroke Fizz.\n\nSon
 oma County artist\, Nancy Gray\, unveils new summer-inspired acrylic paint
 ings that are a colorful expressive interpretation of the region’s beaut
 y.  Summer is the artist’s favorite season and it shows. Drawing inspir
 ation from the French Fauvist tradition\, these works abound with interpre
 tive color choices and bold brush work.  Non-literal color expression pla
 ys out in “Evening Shade” as backlit trees cast blue tendrils of shade
  dancing on a bed of reddish ground.  Sprinkled across a carpet of golden
  yellow\, vibrant red poppies glow in “Sundrenched Splendor\,”amplifyi
 ng the heat of the midday sun.  Red poppies take on a dramatic contrastin
 g role in “Lavender Fields Forever” as they play against the purplish 
 blues and lavenders of the fields and sky.  Inspired by the landscape\, t
 hese works reinterpret it through emotion and memory.  “We are blessed 
 to live amongst Sonoma’s breathtaking scenery – everywhere I look\, I 
 see a painting\,” noted Gray.\n\nGray has had a lifelong passion for art
 .  A Texas native\, she loves living in wine country with its inspiration
 al landscapes.  Along with the Fauvist painters\, early years vacationing
  on the Caribbean Coast and Belize influenced her bright color palette.  
 She began exhibiting her art in Houston in the early 90’s and continued 
 to focus on her painting after moving to Sonoma County.  Gray exhibits re
 gionally and has been a member of the Upstairs Art Gallery for five years.
 \n\nMeet the artist: Gray will host the Gallery on June 18 and 25 from 11a
 m to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Collective Express
 ions: 29 Years\, a members’ collaborative show celebrating the Gallery
 ’s 29th anniversary. Gallery artists offer an exciting mix of mediums\, 
 subject matter and styles emblematic of the Gallery’s dynamic diversity.
   Landscapes by Barretta\, Laland\, and Zorich highlight our region’s b
 eauty\; travel afar with Bird’s Paris cityscape\; from sunflowers to ros
 es\, flowers star in works by Gray\, Haley\, Miller\, Schaffer\, Sumner an
 d Wilson\; succulent oranges are the focus of Stolper’s stunning still-l
 ife\; lovable pets are the subject of Tobin-Charleston’s jewelry\; abstr
 acts by Morgan and Reid bring a moving contemporary complement\; figurativ
 e works by Rapp\, Roney and Shore round out this classic to contemporary o
 verview of the Upstairs artistic family.\n\nAlso join us for ART NITE HEAL
 DSBURG\, Thursday\, June 4\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 
 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and cre
 ativity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\n
 Upstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\
 ) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    www.upstairsart gallery.net 
 \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bv
 drio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
