BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Presented by Bloodroot wines: The Ramble
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T100000
UID:26031904J6EJXH9UaomHkKmzN8ww
DESCRIPTION:ABOUT THE RAMBLE\n\nAn intimate music\, food & wine festival w
 ith purpose. Small by design. Exceptional by nature.\n\nThe Ramble is a bo
 utique music and wine festival in the heart of Sonoma County—curated for
  connection\, discovery\, and impact\, while shining a light on the beauty
  of wine country lifestyle.\n\nCreated by Noah & Kelly Dorrance of BloodRo
 ot and Reeve Wines—music lovers & community ambassadors—The Ramble bri
 ngs together acclaimed artists\, local food and wine\, and a deeply engage
 d audience for a weekend that feels rare\, intentional\, and personal. Fro
 m the beginning\, The Ramble has been committed to giving back. 100% of pr
 oceeds are donated. Impact is not an add-on\, it’s the foundation.\n\n20
 23 featured The Lone Bellow\, SUSTO\, Cayucas\, Spike Sikes & His Awesome 
 Hotcakes\n\n2024 featured Lord Huron\, Andrew Bird\, Cautious Clay\, and T
 he Nude Party\n\n2025 featured Ziggy Marley\, Local Natives\, Richy Mitch 
 & The Coal Miners\, La Luz\, and The Coffis Brothers\n\nVENDORS\n\nAPPLICA
 TIONS ARE NOW OPEN\n\nCalling all vendors! The Ramble is looking for local
  vendors to participate in our many events.\n\nVOLUNTEERS\n\nAPPLICATIONS 
 ARE NOW OPEN\n\nJoin our festival volunteer team! Learn the ropes and hang
  with like-minded music folks. Dates are June 5 - 6!\n\nTHE CAUSE\n\nAll p
 roceeds from the entire weekend will go to helping fight gun violence\, th
 rough our partnership with GIFFORDS\, in honor of our niece\, Evelyn who w
 e lost in the Nashville Covenant School shooting. GIFFORDS is an organizat
 ion dedicated to saving lives from gun violence. Together we inspire the c
 ourage of people from all walks of life to make America safer.
LOCATION:Corazón Healdsburg
URL:https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/presented-by-bloodroot-
 wines-the-ramble/18324480/2026-06-06T10
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Creative Photography Workshop at Jack London State Historic Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T150000
UID:260312kaDL1yHtQUGTcQhpLrFNJQ
DESCRIPTION:Discover and master the potential of your iPhone camera with p
 rofessional photographers **Susan and Neil** Silverman of silvermansphot
 ography.com**.**  \n\nThe first half of the workshop (held inside the Hou
 se of Happy Walls Museum) will cover settings\, filters\, exposure\, focus
 \, shutter speeds\, panoramas\, macro\, close ups\, and portraits\, with a
 n emphasis on the creative and artistic side of photography.  The morning
  venue is reached by a narrow staircase to the second floor. Call 707-938-
 5216 with questions about access.\n\nThe group will then move outdoors to 
 put into practical use the things we have just talked about.  Bring your 
 lunch for a quick picnic.   \n\nParticipants will leave with some potent
 ial great images\, confidence\, and expanded knowledge in using the iPhone
  camera to capture images that are real “keepers.”\n\nAll levels of ph
 otography experience are welcome\, as are both iPhones and Androids (iPhon
 es will be used for demonstrations).
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/iphone-photography-2026/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
