SUMMARY:It's A Grand Night For Singing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T210000
UID:2605084Q8vdQT8b0urjcx20a5CnQ
DESCRIPTION:Each program features fantastic professional vocalists as well
  as the most promising professional talent of tomorrow. Singers from all o
 ver the San Francisco Bay Area \\(and beyond!\\) perform excerpts from ope
 ra\, musical theatre\, cabaret\, and zarzuela -- a plethora of well-loved 
 musical favorites as well as delightful surprises from the lesser known re
 pertoire. \n\nIT'S A GRAND NIGHT FOR SINGING continues the first Saturday
  of every month at 7pm at the Jarvis Conservatory located at 1711 Main Str
 eet in historic downtown Napa. Tickets are $20 and available at the box of
 fice beginning at 6pm\, with doors opening for General Seating at 6:30pm o
 r you may purchase your tickets early online.
LOCATION:Jarvis Conservatory
URL:https://jarvisconservatory.com/iagnfs.html
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Makers Market™ Local Artist Fair @ First Street Napa
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T170000
UID:260505gg7xfnO4006PI5KrVF3g4A
DESCRIPTION:Join Makers Market™ to kick off the 2026 Local Artist Fairs 
 at First Street Napa! Get ready for another season of creativity\, communi
 ty\, and incredible goods made here in the Bay Area. Come support talented
  makers\, discover beautiful artisan products\, and enjoy a fun-filled day
  outdoors!\n\nWHEN? Saturday\, May 9 | 11am - 5pm\n\nWHERE? First Street N
 apa in Napa\, CA\n\n40\\+ local makers\n\nHandmade jewelry\, pottery\, fra
 grances\, candles\, bath and body\, apparel\, leather goods\, and more!\n\
 nKid- and pet-friendly\n\nEnjoy live music by local musicians\n\nStop into
  the Makers Market™ brick-and-mortar store \\(in Suite 301\, adjacent to
  the fair\\) and shop even more unique\, American-made products.\n\nShare 
 with your shopping buddies and mark your calendars! Can't wait to see you 
 there!\n\nAre you a maker looking to sell your products at the Local Artis
 t Street Fair? Register here: https://makersmarket.us/maker-registration/\
 n\nMakers Market is locally founded and independently owned\, with brick-a
 nd-mortar stores in Alpharetta\, Napa\, Santana Row\, Lafayette\, and Mill
  Valley. We aim to bring you products that honor the ideals of American cr
 aftsmanship and are modern\, handmade\, and sustainably produced. Join us 
 in our mission of Rebuilding the Legacy of American Made\, while supportin
 g our local artists\, local economies\, and the community. Come visit one 
 of our stores today! https://makersmarket.us/locations/
LOCATION:First Street Napa
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1770863670938322/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Taste of Italy at Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T170000
UID:260430f640ASvbtkCNtpwGOeKmwQ
DESCRIPTION:For wine drinkers eager to experience world-class wines made i
 n California from Italian varieties\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
  is a must during any trip to Sonoma County. Located just off the plaza in
  the charming town of Healdsburg near famed restaurants\, boutiques and ga
 lleries\, the Centennial Mountain Tasting Room is a destination that invit
 es discovery. Founded by the acclaimed team that guides renowned Pinot Noi
 r and Chardonnay producer Rhys Vineyards\, Centennial Mountain was establi
 shed to explore Italian grape varieties grown on its acclaimed Centennial 
 Mountain Vineyard in the rugged mountains of Northern Sonoma County.\n\nTh
 e Centennial Mountain Vineyard Tasting features the winery’s coveted Neb
 biolo\, and the pioneering Carricante and Nerello Mascalese wines\, among 
 others. To showcase how beautifully the wines pair with food\, the winery 
 also offers a delicious Wine and Sushi Pairing from nearby Asahi Sushi\, o
 ne of Healdsburg’s most popular dining destinations.\n\nGuests can also 
 enhance their tasting experience with a curated salumi board from Journeym
 an Meat Company. This generous accompaniment features six house-made salum
 i\, crostini\, cornichons\, olives\, and a selection of local cheese that 
 serves 2 to 5 guests.
LOCATION:Centennial Mountain Tasting Room
URL:https://cmvineyard.com/visit/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Restorative Yoga
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260606T113000
UID:260427dkt8eBQ060yuwqS6q2KJFg
DESCRIPTION:Begin your summer Saturday mornings with a calming session of 
 restorative yoga at the Garden - an invitation to slow down\, breathe deep
 ly\, and reconnect with yourself in a peaceful natural setting. Whether yo
 u’re looking to unwind from a busy week or manage ongoing stress\, this 
 beginner-friendly class offers a gentle path toward physical and emotional
  balance. Join us to explore the deeply relaxing practices of Yoga Nidra\,
  Yin Yoga\, and restorative postures—all designed to release tension\, c
 alm the nervous system\, and support mindful rest. Classes take place indo
 ors in our Center for Learning & Engagement\, surrounded by the peaceful e
 nergy of the Garden\, it’s the perfect setting to unwind. Sessions are l
 ed by our thoughtful and experienced partners at Sonoma Yoga\, who special
 ize in making yoga both accessible and engaging. These sessions are led by
  our thoughtful and experienced partners at Sonoma Yoga\, a community-cent
 ered studio with over 20 years of experience and a dynamic team of yoga\, 
 fitness\, and meditation guides to support your practice. Please dress acc
 ordingly and bring water.
LOCATION:Sonoma Botanical Garden
URL:https://sonomabg.org/visit/spirit-guides/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
