BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Western Weekend: Celebrating West Marin's Rural Roots
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260607T120000
UID:260520k77EPDfgt0aDqVN4oRHkww
DESCRIPTION:West Marin’s beloved Western Weekend will officially usher
  in summer on June 6 and 7\, celebrating the region's heritage with fresh 
 produce\, Marin Farm Bureau’s famous chicken barbecue\, a barn dance and
  other festivities.\n\nThe event’s centerpiece\, a parade through downto
 wn Point Reyes Station\, will start at 12 noon on Sunday\, June 7. Crowds 
 will line the main street to admire decorated horses\, tractors\, festive 
 floats\, bagpipers\, dancers and more.  The event\, celebrated annually s
 ince 1948\, is free. \n\nCreated to celebrate the rural roots of West Mar
 in\, the annual festival honors our farms\, ranches and villages in an inc
 reasingly urban and fast-paced world. Originally called the West Marin Jun
 ior Livestock Show\, the 77-year-old event is now a broader and more diver
 se celebration of the region.\n\n“This year it's especially important to
  highlight agriculture and what is left of it\, because of those families 
 that we lost\,” following a 2025 settlement that shut down Seashore ranc
 hes\, said Western Weekend’s Junior Grand Marshal Eva Taylor\, 17\, a fi
 fth generation Marin County farmer\, award-winning member of the 2025 Cali
 fornia Shotgun Team and a senior at Tomales High School. \n\nGrand Marsha
 l is historian Dewey Livingston\, 72\, longtime Inverness resident and aut
 hor of the book Point Reyes and Tomales Bay: A History of the Land and It
 s People. \n\nVisitors are urged to come early to avoid traffic detours a
 nd get a good viewing spot. This is a family-friendly and substance-free e
 vent. Bring your refillable water bottle.
LOCATION:downtown Point Reyes Station
URL:https://www.westernweekend.org
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
