 m 3:30 to 5:30 pm. You can drop in for any amount of time. You may continu
 e needle felting and macrame as we now have all of the supplies. We also h
 ave crochet hooks and knitting needles and plenty of yarn to use to learn.
  We will also have tea\, so bring your favorite covered drink container. S
 it and Stitch is for people to come and work on any fiber arts activity th
 at they have while visiting with others. Most people will bring their own 
 projects\, but we always have hooks\, needles\, and yarn and sometimes we 
 will offer a project with instructions that people may choose to make. Let
  us know what you would like to learn this year. We share ideas\, skills\,
  and encouragement with each other. This winter we will be adding sewing\,
  weaving\, and decorative mending to our regular projects of knitting and 
 crocheting. Starting in January\, we will also have a sewing machine avail
 able for use. Children can come if they are accompanied one to one with an
  adult.
