BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Flynn Creek Circus - The Cricket and the Wren
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T210000
UID:260519lTtFJzoZQEG1KqXYYy1vbA
DESCRIPTION:Flynn Creek Circus Presents ‘The Cricket & the Wren’: a hi
 ghly original\, all-human circus that enchants through breathtaking acroba
 tics and athletically stunning skill. Sponsored by the Circus Mentors Inc 
 501c3.\n\nWindsor\, CA— June 11 - 14– This 2026 season\, Flynn Creek C
 ircus invites audiences to ‘The Cricket & the Wren’ — memorable fami
 ly fun and Artful athleticism under the circus big top.\n\nA merchant’s 
 daughter sets out to find the castle where the horizon meets the sea. In o
 rder to  break the spell of the Frog Prince\, she must brave a harrowing 
 journey filled with wonder.\n\nAlong the adventure\, she encounters Jack a
 nd the Beanstalk’s sassy cow\, an out of pocket Pirate and the secret sa
 crifice of the cricket and the wren. \n\nFeaturing aerialists\, jugglers\
 , knife throwers\, and laugh out loud comedy\, this circus blends classic 
 storybook archetypes with imaginative new heroes. The Cricket and the Wren
  will surprise\, dazzle and delight all ages. \n\nIn addition to the fami
 ly friendly showings\,  and the interactive children's camp program held 
 under the circus big top\,  Flynn Creek Circus also presents the wildly p
 opular 'Adults Only Show' boasting outrageous acts\, dark comedy\, and an 
 infamous party atmosphere. Check the website for select adults only showti
 mes as well as special discount nights.\n\nSpectators for all showings are
  invited to the tent to experience the magic up to 30 minutes before each 
 show. The event will offer beer\, wine\, and light concession for purchase
  and include a 15 minute intermission during the two hour show.\n\nLimited
  free parking is available at the location at Keiser Park. \n\nTickets fo
 r Flynn Creek Circus are now available for purchase online at flynncreekci
 rcus.com. Individual ticket prices start at $27 or\, for table reservation
 s\, options start at $98 for two attendees. \n\nFind showtimes and more d
 etails on the camp programs for ages 5-8 and 7-15 at flynncreekcircus.com\
 n\nEarly booking is encouraged for this highly anticipated event.
LOCATION:Keiser Park- Under the Big Top Tent
URL:https://flynncreekcircus.ticketspice.com/2026-windsor-cricket-wren
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: Summertime Livin' Easy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T180000
UID:260519iyjT86J3TU-CbRONy8pKOA
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  5/15/26\n\nJUNE EXHIBIT: SUMMERT
 IME LIVIN’ EASY\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  June 1 – June 28\, 2026\n\nRECEPTI
 ON: SATURDAY\, June 6\, 2026\, 3-6 pm: Join us to meet Nancy Gray  and Ga
 llery artists\;  Learn about their art and celebrate the show and the Gal
 lery’s 29th anniversary.  Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free 
 monthlong drawing for a beautiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments
  will feature the Gallery’s signature mocktail: Brushstroke Fizz.\n\nSon
 oma County artist\, Nancy Gray\, unveils new summer-inspired acrylic paint
 ings that are a colorful expressive interpretation of the region’s beaut
 y.  Summer is the artist’s favorite season and it shows. Drawing inspir
 ation from the French Fauvist tradition\, these works abound with interpre
 tive color choices and bold brush work.  Non-literal color expression pla
 ys out in “Evening Shade” as backlit trees cast blue tendrils of shade
  dancing on a bed of reddish ground.  Sprinkled across a carpet of golden
  yellow\, vibrant red poppies glow in “Sundrenched Splendor\,”amplifyi
 ng the heat of the midday sun.  Red poppies take on a dramatic contrastin
 g role in “Lavender Fields Forever” as they play against the purplish 
 blues and lavenders of the fields and sky.  Inspired by the landscape\, t
 hese works reinterpret it through emotion and memory.  “We are blessed 
 to live amongst Sonoma’s breathtaking scenery – everywhere I look\, I 
 see a painting\,” noted Gray.\n\nGray has had a lifelong passion for art
 .  A Texas native\, she loves living in wine country with its inspiration
 al landscapes.  Along with the Fauvist painters\, early years vacationing
  on the Caribbean Coast and Belize influenced her bright color palette.  
 She began exhibiting her art in Houston in the early 90’s and continued 
 to focus on her painting after moving to Sonoma County.  Gray exhibits re
 gionally and has been a member of the Upstairs Art Gallery for five years.
 \n\nMeet the artist: Gray will host the Gallery on June 18 and 25 from 11a
 m to 6 pm.\n\nThe Stairway Smallworks Showcase features Collective Express
 ions: 29 Years\, a members’ collaborative show celebrating the Gallery
 ’s 29th anniversary. Gallery artists offer an exciting mix of mediums\, 
 subject matter and styles emblematic of the Gallery’s dynamic diversity.
   Landscapes by Barretta\, Laland\, and Zorich highlight our region’s b
 eauty\; travel afar with Bird’s Paris cityscape\; from sunflowers to ros
 es\, flowers star in works by Gray\, Haley\, Miller\, Schaffer\, Sumner an
 d Wilson\; succulent oranges are the focus of Stolper’s stunning still-l
 ife\; lovable pets are the subject of Tobin-Charleston’s jewelry\; abstr
 acts by Morgan and Reid bring a moving contemporary complement\; figurativ
 e works by Rapp\, Roney and Shore round out this classic to contemporary o
 verview of the Upstairs artistic family.\n\nAlso join us for ART NITE HEAL
 DSBURG\, Thursday\, June 4\, 5 – 7 pm.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 
 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is a community event celebrating art and cre
 ativity with over 20 galleries participating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\n
 Upstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Center Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. \\(707\\
 ) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 pm.    www.upstairsart gallery.net 
 \n\nFor further information: Contact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bv
 drio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jamie Lissow
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T000000
UID:260519ZibzIVfPCkqYKk0KwYT0CQ
DESCRIPTION:Actor and comedian Jamie Lissow is currently a regular weekly 
 guest on the \\#1 rated late night talk show\, Gutfeld! on Fox. Jamie is b
 est known for his starring role in two seasons of the Netflix Original Ser
 ies “Real Rob”\, alongside SNL alums Rob Schneider\, Adam Sandler\, No
 rm MacDonald and David Spade\; a show Jamie co-wrote and co-produced.\n\nJ
 amie has appeared on The Tonight Show\, The Late Late Show\, Last Comic St
 anding\, has his own half hour Comedy Central special and a Dry Bar Comedy
  Special with over 20 Million views. Jamie recently wrapped his first movi
 e\, Daddy Daughter Trip\, where he appears alongside John Cleese\, Rob Sch
 neider\, and Micheal Bublé - a movie he co-wrote and produced.\n\nJamie i
 s currently working on the feature film\, The Animal 2\, for Fox/Tubi and 
 continues to headline comedy clubs across the country.
LOCATION:Mystic Theatre & Music Hall
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107464248?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley Pride Weekend Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T220000
UID:2605182BilEaaVjkWHBBI5Y7Mr6g
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma Valley Pride Weekend\n\nSonoma Valley Pride returns for
  a full weekend of queer joy\, live entertainment\, community\, and Pride 
 in the heart of Sonoma Valley.\n\nThis year’s celebration expands into a
  three-day Pride weekend\, bringing together music\, drag\, dancing\, loca
 l artists\, food\, wine\, community organizations\, and LGBTQIA+ visibilit
 y across Sonoma. Sonoma Valley Pride is focused on building queer spaces\,
  creating joyful gathering places\, and bringing more LGBTQIA+ entertainme
 nt and community-centered programming to the region.\n\nThe weekend kicks 
 off Friday\, June 12\, with **We Rise With Pride**\, Sonoma Valley Pride
 ’s first annual Concert and Drag Show at the historic Sebastiani Theatre
 . The evening features headliner **J. Graves**\, a queer\, non-binary-led 
 band from Portland known for their guitar-driven sound\, bold vocals\, and
  high-energy live performances. Blending dance-punk\, post-punk\, and gara
 ge rock influences\, J. Graves brings a sound that will appeal to fans of 
 **Yeah Yeah Yeahs** and **The Kills** — rhythmic\, electric\, and built 
 for the stage. The night also features drag from Bay Area legends **Kochin
 a Rude**\, Sonoma County native\, host\, and performer\, and **Tila Pia**\
 , an infamous stunt queen who has turned looks from Hawaii to New York.\n\
 nOn Saturday\, June 13\, the celebration continues with a Pride Dance Part
 y at **The General’s Daughter**\, inviting the community to keep the wee
 kend moving with music\, dancing\, and celebration.\n\nOn Sunday\, June 14
 \, Sonoma Valley Pride gathers on the historic Sonoma Plaza for a free com
 munity Pride Festival featuring live performances\, speakers\, queer art\,
  local vendors\, food\, wine\, and community connection. With a bigger sta
 ge\, more room to gather\, and even more ways to celebrate\, the Plaza Fes
 tival is designed for friends\, families\, chosen families\, locals\, visi
 tors\, and allies to come together in the spirit of Pride.\n\nFrom the the
 atre to the dance floor to the Plaza lawn\, Sonoma Valley Pride weekend is
  a celebration of queer artistry\, visibility\, belonging\, and joy in Son
 oma Valley. Come ready to dance\, show up\, and be part of what comes next
 .
LOCATION:Sonoma Plaza
URL:https://www.sonomavalleypride.com/?utm_source=press-democrat&utm_mediu
 m=social&utm_campaign=pride-weekend---2026-svp-pride-festival-&utm_content
 =press-dem---weekend-event-listing
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sonoma Valley Pride
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260612T220000
UID:260515VGzUg63uCUqipWWgFfJ6ug
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma Valley Pride returns for a full weekend of queer joy\, 
 live entertainment\, community\, and Pride in the heart of Sonoma Valley.\
 n\nThis year’s celebration expands into a three-day Pride weekend\, brin
 ging together music\, drag\, dancing\, local artists\, food\, wine\, commu
 nity organizations\, and LGBTQIA\\+ visibility across Sonoma. Sonoma Valle
 y Pride is focused on building queer spaces\, creating joyful gathering pl
 aces\, and bringing more LGBTQIA\\+ entertainment and community-centered p
 rogramming to the region.\n\nThe weekend kicks off Friday\, June 12\, with
  We Rise With Pride\, Sonoma Valley Pride’s first annual Concert and Dra
 g Show at the historic Sebastiani Theatre. The evening features headliner 
 J. Graves\, a queer\, non-binary-led band from Portland known for their gu
 itar-driven sound\, bold vocals\, and high-energy live performances. Blend
 ing dance-punk\, post-punk\, and garage rock influences\, J. Graves brings
  a sound that will appeal to fans of Yeah Yeah Yeahs and The Kills — rhy
 thmic\, electric\, and built for the stage. The night also features drag f
 rom Bay Area legends Kochina Rude\, Sonoma County native\, host\, and perf
 ormer\, and Tila Pia\, an infamous stunt queen who has turned looks from H
 awaii to New York.\n\nOn Saturday\, June 13\, the celebration continues wi
 th a Pride Dance Party at The General’s Daughter\, inviting the communit
 y to keep the weekend moving with music\, dancing\, and celebration.\n\nOn
  Sunday\, June 14\, Sonoma Valley Pride gathers on the historic Sonoma Pla
 za for a free community Pride Festival featuring live performances\, speak
 ers\, queer art\, local vendors\, food\, wine\, and community connection. 
 With a bigger stage\, more room to gather\, and even more ways to celebrat
 e\, the Plaza Festival is designed for friends\, families\, chosen familie
 s\, locals\, visitors\, and allies to come together in the spirit of Pride
 .\n\nFrom the theatre to the dance floor to the Plaza lawn\, Sonoma Valley
  Pride weekend is a celebration of queer artistry\, visibility\, belonging
 \, and joy in Sonoma Valley. Come ready to dance\, show up\, and be part o
 f what comes next.
LOCATION:Sonoma Plaza
URL:https://www.sonomavalleypride.com/?utm_source=bohemian&utm_medium=soci
 al&utm_campaign=pride-weekend---2026-svp-pride-festival-&utm_content=svp--
 -bohemian
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
