BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lavender Bloom Fest Open Farm Day
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T160000
UID:260523w2RreygULE2MWcP2cRi-sQ
DESCRIPTION:Mid-May to mid-July is the time when all the lavender at Bees 
 N Blooms is blooming with bright purple radiance\, and we open the farm to
  the public for Lavender Bloom Fest!\n\n**Lavender Bloom Fest Field Days:*
 * May 23\, May 30-31\, June 6-7\, June 13-14\, June 20\,\n\n**Lavender Su
 nset Evenings:** May\, 29\, June 5\, June 12\, June 19\, June 26\n\n**Jaz
 z Days:** May 24\, June 21\, and July 12\n\n**Lavender U-Cut Experience:*
 * June 27-28\, July 4-5\, July 11. Note: July 12 is also a U-Cut day\, bu
 t is listed under Jazz Days.\n\nBring the kids\, visit the poultry palace\
 , play farm bingo\, and snap a picture in the giant lavender chair! Shop t
 he Farm Stand and visit the Bees N Blooms Nursery. Sunset evenings are spe
 cial at Bees N Blooms. Enjoy the view as the suns shines a golden light on
  the lavender. Enjoy dinner with Tacos don Pepe\, then head to the labyrin
 th to watch the sunset.
LOCATION:Bees N Blooms
URL:https://beesnblooms.com/shop/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Staged Reading Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260614T183000
UID:2605122fND9YhcgU-3h83eBaFSpg
DESCRIPTION:This summer\, Valley Players invites you to six unforgettable 
 evenings of theatre — featuring staged readings of bold\, original works
  by both veteran playwrights and emerging talents. Be the first to experie
 nce these sparkling new works brought to life!\n\n**June 14:** *Mother\, I
  Could Kill You* by Barbara A. Silverstone\n\n**June 28:** A Night of One-
 Acts\n\n*When We Ceased to Be?* by Jack Bushnell\n\n*At Midspan on the And
 y Warhol* by Kirk Johnson\n\n**July 12:** *Waldorf School* by Nate Currier
 \n\n**July 26:** *Deadly Pursuits* by Lorraine Midanik\n\n**August 9:** A 
 Night of Shorts\n\n*Madam Director* by Gary A. Davis\n\n*Date Night* by Ba
 rbara A. Silverstone\n\n*Table in the Air* by Rex McGregor\n\n*An Empowere
 d Woman* by Barbara Anderson\n\n**August 23:** *Night Shift* by Mack Wrigh
 t\n\nEach play will be followed by a short talk-back.\n\nBuy tickets onlin
 e and save $3 off the at the door price! Tickets can be pre-purchased onli
 ne or by calling 707-948-6273 for $12 or purchased at the door beginning 3
 0 minutes before showtime for $15.
LOCATION:NVEF Discovery Campus
URL:https://www.valley-players.com/2026/03/06/valley-players-summer-2026-s
 taged-reading-series/
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
