BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The History and Beauty of David Austin® Roses
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T153000
UID:260514YaEeJq_RCkeUDjuDYsfZow
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special afternoon celebrating the beauty and rom
 ance of David Austin® Roses!\n\nWhether you’re a longtime admirer or ju
 st discovering these iconic English roses\, this inspiring program will ex
 plore their rich history\, unforgettable fragrance\, graceful bloom forms\
 , and how to successfully grow them in your own garden. Featuring special 
 guest speaker Rebecca Koraytem of David Austin® Roses USA (BS & MS Hortic
 ulture\; former Southern Living editor\, and award-winning writer & design
 er). \n\nProgram topics include:\n\n• The art & science of rose breedin
 g\n\n• New and notable varieties\n\n• Garden design inspiration\n\n•
  Essential care tips for thriving roses\n\n• Q&A + special drawing to fo
 llow\n\nAll gardening levels welcome—from curious beginners to seasoned 
 rosarians. Space is limited\, so reserve your seat today! sonomaroses.org/
 dar
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Art & Garden Center
URL:https://www.sonomaroses.org/dar
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Back pOrchEstra!- at Murphy's Sonoma June 18\, Thu 7:00-9:00
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T210000
UID:260511HPUXwReKuEWy_irCKXFwQw
DESCRIPTION:American Roots party with Back pOrchEstra!- at Murphy's Sonoma
  June 18\, Thu 7:00-9:00\n\nJoin us for... some Indie and roots rock and t
 he American Roots that inspired it... with Candy Girard\, Tim Eschliman\, 
 Gary Potterton\, Jen Rund and Luis Rodriguez in a mostly-acoustic format o
 n resonator guitar\, violin\, bass\, drums\, percussion\, dobro & Telecast
 er\n\nCelebrating the new "Stories In The Heart" album\, listen now!: http
 s://orcd.co/5xga7nr\n\nSingle out now too\, "Ever Think About It:" https:/
 /orcd.co/qo5579q\n\nLPs\, CDs\, and USB-Music Cards available all over\, i
 ncluding https://www.globerecords.com\n\nVince's Hot Picks (Best of 2026):
  "... a warm\, road-worn album that leans into rich acoustic tones while f
 reely bending genres without ever breaking the feel. Built around a mostly
  unplugged framework\, the record draws from country blues\, roots rock\, 
 Zydeco\, Tex-Mex\, New Orleans rhythms\, Motown soul\, singer-songwriter t
 raditions\, and even Brazilian textures\, all woven together with an easy 
 confidence that sounds earned\, not assembled."\n\n464 1st St E\, Sonoma\,
  CA 95476 (707) 935-0660 ...with plenty of outdoor seating that includes b
 oth Murphy's Irish Pub and Taste of the Himalayas.\n\n...songs from all ov
 er the map... originals and reworked classics by Hank Williams\, Taj Mahal
 \, Dan Hicks\, Big Bill Broonzy\, Bob Wills\, Jimmy Reed\, Joseph & Cleome
  Falcon and Bobby Charles.\n\nwhat a sample? check out the "Dusty Road I'm
  On" video: https://youtu.be/jj0IIkUyrE4 ...a twangy roots rock number wit
 h a Cajun flavor and hints of Jesse Ed Davis and Sid Page....\n\n"...every
 thing from alt. rock to cajun\, to country\, to Brownie Ford era Western S
 wing. But the thing that keeps this set together is their excellent songwr
 iting full of smooth never-miss-a-beat lines and vivid imagery. It's a stu
 dio album but it sure does have a back porch jam band feel to it" - Calvin
  Powers\, WHUP-FM\, americanamusicshow.com\,\n\nmore at... https://www.Bac
 kpOrchEstra.com\n\nBandCamp: https://backporchestra.bandcamp.com\n\nyouTub
 e: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLOTwG2XEiO2O8c0dEI-7hlpI8nr7apiN
 f\n\nBluesky: https://bsky.app/profile/backporchestra.bsky.social\n\nRever
 b Nation: https://www.reverbnation.com/backporchestra\n\nFacebook: https:/
 /www.facebook.com/BackPorchEstra/\n\nInstagram: https://www.instagram.com/
 backporchestra/\n\n#rootsrock\n\n#americanrootsmusic\n\n#americanamusic\n\
 n#rockabillymusic\n\n#twangyguitar\n\n#backporchestra\n\n#acousticmusic\n\
 n#adultalbumalternative\n\n#singersongwriter\n\n#folkmusic\n\n#folkrock
LOCATION:Murphys Irish Pub
URL:https://www.BackpOrchEstra.com#cal
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wine Tails Trail at Cuvaison Winery
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T170000
UID:2605087Z2_dPxrYkWdTlLxbj-vwQ
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy a new way to experience Cuvaison with your canine compan
 ion on the Wine Tails Trail. This self-guided vineyard walk winds just und
 er a mile through our Los Carneros estate\, with QR code stops highlightin
 g the history of our vines and winemaking. Guests begin their adventure by
  checking in with our Concierge for a map and orientation before setting o
 ff on the trail.\n\nAfter the walk\, return to the estate and enjoy a seat
 ed tasting of our current release wines\, while your pup relaxes by your s
 ide and enjoys a selection of “Barkuterie.” The Wine Tails Trail is a 
 chance to stretch your legs\, explore the vineyard\, and savor Cuvaison in
  the company of your best friend.\n\nWhen booking this experience\, please
  plan for the dog walk to begin at the time you select. The walk itself av
 erages about 45 minutes\, though you’ll also check in with our Concierge
  before and after\, as well as complete a quick waiver at the start. Your 
 wine tasting will be scheduled 60 minutes after your selected walk time\, 
 allowing a smooth transition from the trail back to your seated experience
 .\n\nGroup Size: Up to 4 guests\, including non-tasters\n\nDuration: Pleas
 e allow 120 minutes for this experience
LOCATION:Cuvaison Experience Salon\, Outdoors Only
URL:https://tewines.com/pages/cuvaison-tastings 
